<%#
  Pagination, rendered in the table card's footer slot:

    render "shared/essentials/card", padded: false,
           footer: essentials_pagination_footer(@paginated_things) do

  It draws no border and no padding of its own -- the card footer already supplies
  `border-t border-slate-200 px-5 py-3`. It used to draw both, which put the pager inside two
  stacked hairlines twelve pixels apart on every page that used the footer slot.

  A table that is not the card's last child -- a tab panel, say -- supplies that chrome itself,
  by assigning essentials_pagination_footer to a local and wrapping it in the same div.

  Go through the helper either way. It returns nil for a single-page collection, which is what
  keeps the card from drawing an empty strip.

  The wrapper is a div, not a nav: kaminari's own paginator emits the nav landmark labelled
  "Pagination", and nesting one inside another gives a screen-reader user two identically
  named landmarks for the same control.
%>
<% if collection.respond_to?(:total_pages) && collection.total_pages > 1 %>
  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3">
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-600">
      <%= essentials_pagination_summary(collection) %>
    </p>
    <%= paginate collection, params: (defined?(page_params) ? page_params : {}) %>
  </div>
<% end %>
